          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Does homeowners insurance cover foundation crack repair?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Usually not when the cause is settling, shrinkage, soil pressure or gradual wear, which most policies exclude. Coverage may apply if the damage results from a covered sudden event, such as a burst pipe, depending on your policy. Read your policy and talk to your agent before assuming either way, since wording varies between insurers and states."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How long does foundation crack injection last?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "A properly done injection on a stable crack typically lasts for the life of the wall, which is why many contractors offer long or lifetime warranties on the repaired crack. Failures usually come from poor surface sealing, incomplete filling or a crack that is still moving. New cracks elsewhere in the wall are not covered by that repair."
          }
        },
