          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Most crack injection is done from the inside, and it works well because the resin fills the crack through the wall's full thickness. Bracing methods like carbon fiber and steel beams are also interior. Exterior work is generally reserved for full waterproofing, wall rebuilding or situations where the inside cannot be accessed."
          }
