        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            A typical leaking foundation crack costs roughly 250 to 800 dollars to inject professionally, or about 50 to 130 dollars to do yourself with a kit. A bowing basement wall is a different budget, usually several thousand dollars per wall for carbon fiber, steel beams or anchors, and more if the wall must be rebuilt.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The single most valuable step is figuring out which kind of crack you have before you pay for a fix. Monitor it, call an engineer for anything horizontal, wide, offset or growing, and fix the drainage that caused it. Then seal the wall with one of our <a href="/best-foundation-sealer/" class="text-[#1E90FF] font-semibold hover:underline">best foundation sealer</a> picks.
          </p>
